-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Sep 22 13:53:25 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 0.38.0:
  * New headroom-cache-ttl command: offline estimator that turns
    recorded cache observations into a learned TTL table for
    providers that do not publish a cache TTL
  * Bound decompressed request bodies and cap the
    /admin/runtime-env request body at 64 KiB, closing two proxy
    denial-of-service paths
  * New headroom telemetry command prints what the opt-out
    beacon sends; the beacon payload widens to cache, session
    and configuration counters
  * Match the Bearer auth scheme case-insensitively (RFC 7235)
  * Proxy accepts the OpenAI Responses shape on the gateway turn
    and enforces budget limits on the OpenAI and Gemini routes
  * Compression preserves Bash control flow and pauses AST
    compression per language after repeated invalid-syntax
    discards; file-read tool output stays byte-exact
  * Dashboard gains a Cost Saved headline card, routing savings
    and keyboard-operable controls
  * Write per-port proxy logs so concurrent instances stop
    truncating each other
  * Vendored rustls updated to 0.23.45 for RUSTSEC-2026-0285 and
    tree-sitter to 0.27.0
  * Many more fixes and improvements; see upstream's release
    notes for the full list
- Follow upstream and raise the litellm requirement to 1.96.2,
  now unconditional on the Python version

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Sep  8 16:36:22 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Initial package 0.37.0: core CLI built with maturin (pyo3
  headroom._core)
  * Requires distro ast-grep rather than the ast-grep-cli PyPI
    wheel; binaries.resolve() searches PATH
  * ExclusiveArch rust_tier1_arches; crates vendored with
    cargo_vendor mode=manual
  * headroom-proxy subpackage is headroom-ai[proxy]: FastAPI,
    uvicorn, magika, onnxruntime, sqlite-vec, and the rest of
    the CLI gate (ensure_proxy_dependencies)
  * headroom-proxy is noarch (Requires-only extra)

